Jalung: Sirrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrraaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.
Sira: Hey, Jalung.
Jalung: We gotta tighten up our security because of you now.
Sira: Yeah, sorry about that.
Jalung: Eeehhh, it's no worries. At least I have Nyanggau to talk to.
Sira: He talks?
Jalung: Well.
Jalung: "Talk" as in, I do all the talking and he listens.
Sira: How does he even put up with you all day?
Jalung: Psshh, he likes it.
Jalung: Right, Nyanggau?
Nyanggau: ...
Jalung: See? He likes it.
Sira: Riiight...
if {manuk_pansuh} == true:
	Sira: Anyways, Jalung.
	Jalung: Yah?
	Sira: Have you...
	Sira: Have you ever seen a group of shadows in the Sacred Forest?
	Jalung: Group of shadows?
	*Jalung scratches his chin*
	Jalung: ...
	Jalung: I think I might have...
	Jalung: But I thought they were a bunch of animals.
	Sira: When was this?
	Jalung: Some time around when I found Jitendra falling from a tree.
	*Sira crosses her arms together, a deeply uncomfortable feeling weighs down her chest*
	Jalung: Why do you ask?
	Sira: Nope. Nothing. Enjoy standing around doing nothing all day, Jalung.
	Jalung: *groans loudly in protest before going back to his post*